ule is very  very important in order to determine  whether it's a cancerous nodule also we  add some extra attributes like XY and Z  location and the distance to the lung  border which are also of great help in  determining whether whether something  else whether a lung nodule is cancerous  and here you couldn't see the model that  we implemented on top of those  attributes that I spoke to you about  earlier and as you can see it's very  easy to implement it's only a few lines  of dense flow code and that that's why  we use sense flow a lot it's a really  good help at what we do and it basically  has everything that we need so we will  fit a linear model but we apply modern  techniques like dropout and noise on top  of it and because we have a lot of  candidates per scan we want to reduce  all the scandals to a certain probe to  one single probability and the way we do  is take by taking the maximum loss loss  over the candidates so with right here  you can see the reduce max function  which is exactly what that does it takes  the maximum over all the linear models  which are defined here so we multiply  the input by weights and Adam bias and  then we take the maximum and then with  built-in function from tens flow we can  calculate the cross entropy and minimize  that and so in only few lines of code  you can create powerful models that you  wouldn't be able to create in order  frameworks  okay finally some comments what deep  learning is awesome for medical imaging  it's it's going to revolutionize the  industry and well we will we are already  seeing great results from it and there's  so much more to do and test out on these  data sets that are huge and that is  that's just discrete these techniques  are are essential to to creating the  performance that we obtain also the size  and quality of our data is very  important as you can see with the cattle  competition we only have 1300 scans if  you would have half a million scans  there's no limits to what we could 